        <section class="granite-section" aria-labelledby="granite-product-title">
          <div class="granite-section-intro"><p class="granite-kicker">Choose the actual product</p><h2 id="granite-product-title">Three names that lead to different results</h2><p>“Crushed granite” tells you the parent rock. It does not tell you the size distribution or whether the load contains fines. Ask the yard for the screened size and gradation.</p></div>
          <figure class="granite-figure">
            <img src="/crushed-granite-grades.svg" alt="Cross-section comparing open spaces in clean angular granite, a dense mix with fines, and fine decomposed granite" width="960" height="420" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>Granite grade changes how the layer behaves. The diagram explains particle arrangement; it is not an installation specification. Scroll horizontally to read it on a narrow screen.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="granite-choice-grid">
            <div class="granite-choice"><span>01 · Open graded</span><h3>Clean crushed granite</h3><p>Screened angular pieces leave connected voids. Choose a specified clean grade for drainage layers or another design that needs infiltration. A loose unpaved driving surface may move under tires.</p><a href="/drain-rock-calculator">Estimate a clean drainage layer →</a></div>
            <div class="granite-choice"><span>02 · Dense graded</span><h3>Granite with fines</h3><p>Smaller fragments fill the gaps between coarse pieces. A properly graded surface can bind and compact more firmly for a traditional unpaved drive. Ask for a road-surface or base product suited to your site.</p><a href="/crushed-stone-calculator">Compare crushed-stone grades →</a></div>
            <div class="granite-choice"><span>03 · Fine material</span><h3>Decomposed granite</h3><p>DG is a finer path and patio material, sometimes sold as “crushed granite fines.” It has its own product weights and installation details. Confirm the name on the quote before using this coarse-stone estimate.</p><a href="/decomposed-granite-calculator">Use the DG calculator →</a></div>
          </div>
